{"id": "EUVD-2026-76258", "enisaUuid": "68676833-e79f-3c03-beb9-5beede30bf2e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7996: bound the device EEPROM address before the EFUSE copy\n\nmt7996_mcu_get_eeprom() derives the destination of the EFUSE/EXT block\ncopy from the address reported by the MCU response (event->addr, a\ndevice-controlled __le32) and clamps only the copy length, never the\ndestination offset into dev->mt76.eeprom.data. A malicious or\nmalfunctioning device can report an arbitrary address and drive an\nout-of-bounds write of up to MT7996_EXT_EEPROM_BLOCK_SIZE bytes past\neeprom.data.\n\nReject a response whose address would place the copy outside eeprom.data\nbefore deriving the destination pointer. Devices that echo the requested\nin-bounds offset are unaffected.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:47:15", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4892be1ef0bbe6db6b13bf46cb79b6706bb5b214", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/388f471ca4758f644394b681ce97677a4d0e772c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9e5abb5e2ade0b6fd0e47209711115d47a255176", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6be59da2063d5b3522bfde8aae0487ec095eb384", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/13b3c29a782033ce4a230be9e5618032813dbcd4"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80935", "GHSA-gmwf-mx64-6gvq"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.4, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "226853a4-007c-332c-b1e7-6a71eed3b47d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "98686cd21624c75a043e96812beadddf4f6f48e5 <4892be1ef0bbe6db6b13bf46cb79b6706bb5b214"}, {"id": "231f39f9-a12a-3561-a678-bbb3d6c5180a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "411fa529-ec4e-341d-8ba8-e423c78a07c9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"